{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-52524",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that the first term of the sequence is ${a}_{1}=-1.$\n\nInspecting the terms of the sequence, we see that we always get the next term by dividing by $-2.$ This is the same as multiplying by $-\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the recursive rule must be the following:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=-1\n$$\n\nSo, the missing values are $-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $-1.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
